# ShellCheck, the POSIX sh quarter of this repository's gate. `[workspace.lints]` in
# `Cargo.toml` does this job for Rust, `ruff.toml` for Python and
# `PSScriptAnalyzerSettings.psd1` for PowerShell.
#
# **Standing order, Terry, 2026-08-17**, global rather than this project's: every language in
# a project gets a best-of-breed linter at best-practice pedantry, XOR a written override
# from Terry. He confirmed the same day: *"yeah def install LSP and linter(s) to get good
# coverage."*
#
# **There is exactly one shell script here, and it is `.githooks/pre-commit` — the gate
# itself.** That is why one file is worth a linter: a bug in the hook does not fail loudly,
# it silently stops the other three languages being checked at all. It is the one script in
# this repository whose failure mode is *every other check quietly not running*.
#
# **No language server, same as PowerShell.** The official plugin marketplace ships twelve
# and none for shell. Checked 2026-08-17.
#
#     shellcheck .githooks/pre-commit
#
# **The survey**, `--severity=style --enable=all`, the maximum: **5 findings**. Three
# families, and all three are answered below rather than suppressed silently. At the default
# setting only SC2016 fires.

# Everything optional is on. `--enable=all` turns on the opt-in checks, and with the two
# exclusions below it reports NOTHING here -- so maximum pedantry costs nothing today and
# catches the next one for free.
enable=all

# SC2310 -- "this function is invoked in an 'if' condition so set -e will be disabled".
#
# **That is the control flow, not an accident.** `touched` exists to answer yes or no, and a
# `grep -qE` that finds nothing exits 1. Invoking it "separately", as the check suggests,
# would make `set -e` abort the hook the first time a commit did not touch Rust -- turning
# every docs-only commit into a failed one. The check is right about the mechanism and wrong
# about whether it is wanted.
disable=SC2310

# SC2250 -- "prefer putting braces around variable references even when not strictly
# required". Pure style, opt-in only, and the surrounding script does not use braces. A
# linter that reformats a working script to its own taste is the noise the other three
# configs in this repository all refuse.
disable=SC2250

# **SC2016 is NOT disabled here.** It fires once, on the single-quoted PowerShell block, and
# it is answered with an inline `# shellcheck disable` at that line so the check stays live
# for every other string in the file. A global disable would wave through a genuine
# `'$missing'` somewhere else.
